## Fix 5 — collapse duplicated resolution body (also fixes an inconsistency)

**File**: `cmd/entire/cli/cell_target.go`

`resolveRepoCellTarget`'s owner/repo branch and `resolveRepoCellPlacement` currently run near-identical bodies (`newCellCoreClient` → `resolveProcessingPlacement` → `cellTargetForClusterSlug`), justified by a comment saying they return different shapes. That justification doesn't hold — returning a superset is free — and the duplication has a real cost: only `resolveRepoCellPlacement` routes failures through `cellPlacementError`, which gives a distinguishable "timed out" message. So today a hung control plane produces a clearly-labeled timeout error for `explain --repo` but an unlabeled generic error for `entire trail`/`entire experts`.

**Fix**: have `resolveRepoCellTarget`'s owner/repo path call `resolveRepoCellPlacement` and discard the id:
```go
func resolveRepoCellTarget(ctx context.Context, fullName, ulid string) (*auth.CellTarget, error) {
	if strings.TrimSpace(ulid) != "" {
		ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(ctx, requiredCellResolveTimeout)
		defer cancel()
		c, err := newCellCoreClient()
		if err != nil {
			return nil, fmt.Errorf("control plane unavailable: %w", err)
		}
		repo, err := c.GetRepo(ctx, coreapi.GetRepoParams{RepoId: ulid})
		if err != nil {
			return nil, fmt.Errorf("resolve the Entire cell for %s: %w", ulid, err)
		}
		clusterHost := strings.TrimSpace(repo.ClusterHost.Or(""))
		if clusterHost == "" {
			return nil, fmt.Errorf("resolve the Entire cell for %s: repo has no cluster host", ulid)
		}
		target, err := cellTargetForClusterHost(ctx, c, clusterHost)
		if err != nil {
			return nil, fmt.Errorf("resolve the Entire cell for %s: %w", ulid, err)
		}
		return target, nil
	}

	owner, repo, ok := strings.Cut(strings.TrimSpace(fullName), "/")
	if !ok || owner == "" || repo == "" {
		return nil, fmt.Errorf("invalid repo %q: expected owner/repo", fullName)
	}
	placement, err := resolveRepoCellPlacement(ctx, owner, repo)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return placement.Target, nil
}
```
Note the top-level `context.WithTimeout(ctx, requiredCellResolveTimeout)` moves to be scoped to the ULID branch only, since the owner/repo branch now delegates to `resolveRepoCellPlacement`, which applies its own identical timeout independently — don't double-wrap ctx for that path. Update `resolveRepoCellTarget`'s doc comment to reflect that the owner/repo path is now literally `resolveRepoCellPlacement` plus discarding the id (state the actual reason the two functions still exist separately: different return shape for different callers, not different resolution logic).

While here: `cellPlacementError`'s message says `"resolving the Entire mirror for %s/%s timed out"` — "mirror" is a holdover from the old mirrors-scanning implementation. Since this now serves `entire trail`/`entire experts` too (not just `explain --repo`), consider renaming to `"resolving the Entire cell for %s/%s timed out"` for accuracy — optional polish, your call, but if you skip it leave a note why.

Re-verify all existing `resolveRepoCellTarget`/`resolveRepoCellPlacement` tests still pass after this restructuring — some error-message-content assertions may need adjusting if wording changed (e.g. anything asserting the exact non-timeout error text for the owner/repo path, if such an assertion exists — check).

